// Turn the logo files pulled off the running containers into Rust constants.
// 
// WHY THE LOGOS ARE FETCHED RATHER THAN DRAWN. Hand-drawing a brand mark from
// memory does not produce that brand's logo, it produces a wrong one. Every mark
// here came out of the container that actually runs the app -- Tandoor's from
// Tandoor, Grafana's from Grafana -- so the icon on the card is the real mark of
// the software behind it.
// 
// WHAT THIS HAS TO FIX. The templates render `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">{icon}</svg>`
// in eighteen places, so an icon must be INNER svg content that behaves inside a
// 24x24 box. Three things get in the way, and all three are silent:
// 
//   1. IDS AND CLASS NAMES ARE GLOBAL once inlined. Tandoor's gradients are
//      `XMLID_5_`; Grafana ships a `<style>` block full of `.st0`. Drop two of
//      those on one page and the second logo repaints the first. Every id and
//      class is prefixed with the brand name here.
//   2. THE SURROUNDING CSS SETS stroke: currentColor AND fill: none, which
//      inherit into the logo and turn a filled mark into an outline of itself.
//      A `stroke="none"` on the wrapper blocks the stroke; the marks carry their
//      own fill attributes, which beat an inherited value.
//   3. VIEWBOXES ARE ALL DIFFERENT -- 640, 512, 351x365, 70x84. Each is scaled
//      to fit 24 and centred, rather than assuming a square.
// 
// PNG marks (Immich, it-tools, openGym, Homepage) ship no vector anywhere in
// their images. They are downscaled to 64px and embedded as a data URI inside an
// `<image>` element, which ignores fill and stroke entirely. A real logo slightly
// soft beats a wrong logo drawn sharply.

#![allow(dead_code)]

